.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/
data/raw/*
!data/raw/MANIFEST.json
data/interim/*
data/processed/*
!data/**/.gitkeep
# Figures are tracked, not ignored: the technical report embeds them, so they
# have to travel with the source that cites them and be visible in a diff when a
# run changes them. Only the full run writes there; a --quick run writes to
# outputs/quick/, which is ignored, so the CI path cannot quietly replace a
# figure with one that disagrees with outputs/metrics.json.
outputs/quick/
outputs/**/*.pdf
.ipynb_checkpoints/
sbi-logs/

# Built video: reproduced by `make video` from the tracked stills.
outputs/video/frames/
outputs/video/frames.txt

# Explainers written for readers without a machine-learning background. Kept out
# of the repository at the author's request; they are companions to
# report/TECHNICAL_REPORT.md, not part of the submission. `report.verify` and the
# clinical-language test still check them locally, because a document that quotes
# numbers should be held to the same rule whether or not it ships.
report/MODELLING_FOR_BIOLOGISTS.md
report/DIGITAL_TWIN_FOR_BIOLOGISTS.md
